flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1{"Does the part meet quality assurance team product<br/>specifications?"}
    box_2["Check product dimensions and inspect for static<br/>charge and contamination."]
    box_3["Remove the non conforming parts from the supply and<br/>reload with a product batch that meets quality<br/>assurance team specifications."]
    box_4{"Is the part supply from the hopper correct?"}
    box_5["Complete the following checks: 1. Check whether<br/>parts exit the hopper evenly. 2. Check the feed<br/>opening for too many or too few parts. 3. Check<br/>whether parts are undamaged on exit from the hopper."]
    box_6[/"Hopper part supply diagnostic procedure"/]
    box_7{"Is the part supply to the assembly robot gripper<br/>correct?"}
    box_8["Complete the following checks: 1. Check whether<br/>parts are evenly distributed across the belt. 2.<br/>Check whether the supply belt runs stably without<br/>jerky movements. 3. Check that parts do not shift<br/>during belt transport (use a high speed camera if<br/>necessary)."]
    box_9[/"Part supply belt diagnostic procedure"/]
    box_10{"Is the vision working correctly?"}
    box_11["Complete the following steps: 1. Check in the vision<br/>system application whether products are correctly<br/>recognised. 2. If recalibration is needed, refer to<br/>the vision coordinate assignment procedure."]
    box_12[/"Vision coordinate assignment procedure (verify<br/>camera lens is secure)"/]
    box_13{"Are there contaminated parts?"}
    box_14["Complete the following checks: 1. Check whether the<br/>vacuum head is contaminated. 2. Check the vacuum<br/>filter for contamination. 3. Check vacuum for<br/>leakage (see pneumatic flow measurement procedure<br/>for values). 4. Check whether the assembly robot<br/>axes are contaminated. 5. Check the centering sleeve<br/>for contamination relative to the vacuum tube."]
    box_15["Clean the parts and clean or replace the vacuum<br/>filter as needed."]
    box_16[/"Assembly robot axis lubrication procedure"/]
    box_17{"Are there electrical defects?"}
    box_18["Complete the following checks: 1. Check the cabling<br/>and proximity sensor actuator. 2. Check whether the<br/>vacuum generator works correctly. 3. Check system<br/>settings on the operator control interface."]
    box_19["Replace the defective cabling and/or sensor, and the<br/>generator if faulty."]
    box_20{"Are there worn parts?"}
    box_21["Complete the following checks: 1. Check wear on the<br/>vacuum tube. 2. Check wear on the actuator centering<br/>sleeve. 3. Check the assembly robot axes for wear.<br/>4. Check smooth movement of the centering sleeve<br/>relative to the vacuum tube (by disconnecting the<br/>actuator)."]
    box_22["Replace the worn components identified in the<br/>inspection (vacuum tube, centering sleeve, and/or<br/>assembly robot axes)."]
    box_23[/"Assembly robot replacement procedure"/]
    box_24{"Is the extended position of the centering sleeve<br/>relative to the vacuum tube correct?"}
    box_25[/"Refer to the centering sleeve extended position<br/>check for variant A machines (small format parts)."/]
    box_26[/"Refer to the centering sleeve extended position<br/>check for variant B machines (medium format parts)."/]
    box_27[/"Refer to the centering sleeve extended position<br/>check for variant C machines (large format parts)."/]
    box_28["Adjust the actuator end stop to set the correct<br/>extended position of the centering sleeve relative<br/>to the vacuum tube."]
    box_29{"Height of centering sleeve relative to supply belt<br/>correct?"}
    box_30[/"Refer to the centering sleeve height relative to<br/>supply belt for variant A machines (small format<br/>parts)."/]
    box_31[/"Refer to the centering sleeve height relative to<br/>supply belt for variant B machines (medium format<br/>parts)."/]
    box_32[/"Refer to the centering sleeve height relative to<br/>supply belt for variant C machines (large format<br/>parts)."/]
    box_33["Set the Z height of the assembly robot to position<br/>the centering sleeve at the correct height relative<br/>to the supply belt."]
    box_34{"Part pick up position from supply conveyor correct?"}
    box_35["Complete the following checks: 1. Check x/y/z pickup<br/>position(s) using a high speed camera (see assembly<br/>robot supply pickup adjustment procedure). 2. Verify<br/>the part is correctly centred under the vacuum head.<br/>3. Monitor the number of retry attempts."]
    box_36["Complete the following checks: 1. Using jogging<br/>mode, verify that picking up the part from the<br/>supply conveyor is correct and that the part is<br/>correctly aligned under the vacuum head. 2. Check<br/>whether the assembly robot produces excessive<br/>retries when picking up the part."]
    box_37[/"Robot vision supply integration adjustment procedure"/]
    box_38(["Picking up part from supply conveyor is correct"])

